<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>World | Deutsche Welle</title><subtitle type="html">World | Deutsche Welle</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-world</id><updated>2026-09-11T12:54:51Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-world" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-world" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Iran war: Saudi-Houthi escalation intensifies Yemen conflict</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ccf3915372e320ce7264f51657476a3e4e55c0cfa8bf471659f0f655bbd808f6</id><updated>2026-09-11T12:54:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T11:52:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iran-war-saudi-houthi-escalation-intensifies-yemen-conflict/a-79226627--c5b66c310724.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iran-war-saudi-houthi-escalation-intensifies-yemen-conflict/a-79226627?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Houthi takeovers of Mokha, Dhubab and Perim in the Bab el-Mandeb Strait threaten to push Yemen deeper into the Middle East war. The Iran-backed group has made advances against Yemen's government and Saudi Arabia.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Why North Korea's Kim Jong Un doesn't need a US deal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:daeb60e067d52da3910e84d8cb71f88bb059e503d80d21cb8c7cde6b965ae6cc</id><updated>2026-09-11T12:54:23Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T10:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-north-korea-s-kim-jong-un-doesn-t-need-a-us-deal/a-79227854--e7f102464964.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-north-korea-s-kim-jong-un-doesn-t-need-a-us-deal/a-79227854?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Donald Trump's overtures to North Korea's dictator have gone nowhere, with an emboldened Pyongyang accelerating its nuclear program and solidifying alliances with Russia and China.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Turks in Germany anxious after AfD wins in Saxony-Anhalt</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e903fef67c19d3806aebb4ce4034d65a75f577ed766b70437d7f5512541cd178</id><updated>2026-09-11T12:54:29Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T10:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/turks-in-germany-anxious-after-afd-wins-in-saxony-anhalt/a-79221764--9bdd69d84853.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/turks-in-germany-anxious-after-afd-wins-in-saxony-anhalt/a-79221764?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Alternative for Germany party's win in Saxony-Anhalt has alarmed people of Turkish origin in eastern states. Will workers and business owners abandon the increasingly AfD-friendly region for the more welcoming west?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Hong Kong Tiananmen activists jailed for up to 7 years</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8edb2a41aeefd93620a1cbe9bef11cd856b92e88931b5fcc8b6c54ad305b1e9d</id><updated>2026-09-11T12:54:42Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T08:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/hong-kong-tiananmen-activists-jailed-for-up-to-7-years/a-79224243--b40cd2f6f0ea.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/hong-kong-tiananmen-activists-jailed-for-up-to-7-years/a-79224243?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Three pro-democracy activists who organized annual commemorations of China's deadly 1989 Tiananmen crackdown were charged under Hong Kong's Beijing-backed national security law.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Magyar vs. Moscow: Hungary's new tough stance toward Russia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:98329643596d99af9ab671e6fccc1b9852733cefb9da4af8441d94bb7caaf54f</id><updated>2026-09-11T12:54:45Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T08:20:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/magyar-vs-moscow-hungary-s-new-tough-stance-toward-russia/a-79223424--11535ff26ff5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/magyar-vs-moscow-hungary-s-new-tough-stance-toward-russia/a-79223424?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Hungarian PM Peter Magyar has abruptly ended the era of his predecessor's warm relations with Russia: Budapest has expelled 10 Russian diplomats from the country. Moscow is considering halting gas supplies in response.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Philippines ferry fire: Search continues for dozens missing</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:513e0b8792c95091be9ce4b909f78ff969d02bf67d657a030d21f664de73f523</id><updated>2026-09-11T12:54:48Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T08:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/philippines-ferry-fire-search-continues-for-dozens-missing/a-79223425--fc38c9af4128.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/philippines-ferry-fire-search-continues-for-dozens-missing/a-79223425?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Firefighters searching for survivors combed through the smoking remains of a ferry off the coast of Coron island in the Philippines. Five people died and over 40 have been rescued</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's connection to the 9/11 attacks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:359678b7a879278cfecfc96046dcec23543ff3886a63d7ab50c9fd0b79689ae3</id><updated>2026-09-11T12:54:51Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T06:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-connection-to-the-9-11-attacks/a-79202918--33622f8e5007.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-connection-to-the-9-11-attacks/a-79202918?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The 9/11 plot, including the twin tower attacks, was partly planned by the so-called Hamburg cell. A look at how Germany's national security was reshaped.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Digital data leeches: Trading on our profiles</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5d87a9de7213dbe6e8c7d9d876b9ee92de8946314eeb77660f86f013c7840f9f</id><updated>2026-09-11T12:53:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T19:08:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/digital-data-leeches-trading-on-our-profiles/a-79219770--a0160555e43f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/digital-data-leeches-trading-on-our-profiles/a-79219770?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">US tech companies gather, link, and sell more and more information about their users. The scandal involving the dating app Grindr shows how easy it is for highly sensitive data to fall into the wrong hands.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>25 years after 9/11: Al-Qaeda weakened but not gone</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:681c0fd6a3e5d05b35a2a1058c6dfb000e98bf6864e5f30bdf108f83cff00814</id><updated>2026-09-11T12:53:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T18:05:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/25-years-after-9-11-al-qaeda-weakened-but-not-gone/a-79202457--b51e1f0501b8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/25-years-after-9-11-al-qaeda-weakened-but-not-gone/a-79202457?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">25 years after 9/11, the terrorist group al-Qaeda is no longer the global terrorist organization it once was. Its central leadership has been weakened, but offshoots remain strong across Africa and Asia.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Germany’s Goethe-Institut is closing in Russia. Russians tell DW how canceled exams are upending their plans</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:beaf92a33b0e4bb231582cab3a4563228b539083d01c835e279e330ac55ef4cd</id><updated>2026-09-11T12:53:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T16:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-goethe-institut-is-closing-in-russia-russians-tell-dw-how-canceled-exams-are-upending-thei/a-79218936--791b0bcb39e0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-goethe-institut-is-closing-in-russia-russians-tell-dw-how-canceled-exams-are-upending-their-plans/a-79218936?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Canceled language exams, disrupted plans to study in Germany and the disappearance of an important cultural link: DW users shared how the closure of Germany's Goethe-Institut in Russia affects their lives.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>African Parks: when conservation becomes a question of power</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:00e5a2d1c24bc59d150512c67bcc6b1902c1ac8c3a270e2aa8f1832daec79f4d</id><updated>2026-09-11T12:53:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T15:24:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/african-parks-when-conservation-becomes-a-question-of-power/a-78914372--4689a2636f76.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/african-parks-when-conservation-becomes-a-question-of-power/a-78914372?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">African Parks is dedicated to protecting wildlife on the continent across some vast areas. But the organization faces allegations of human rights abuses by rangers. Now Prince Harry is stepping down from its board.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
